    "problem_statement": "The LwM2M library lacks a way to query how many samples can still be stored in a cached resource. A caller should be able to ask, for a given object path, how many free slots remain in that resource's cache (to decide when to flush buffered samples via lwm2m_send), receiving the count on success or a negative errno. When resource data cache support is not configured, the query must fail with -ENOTSUP, and querying with a NULL path must fail with -EINVAL.",
